  >>> t2 = tf.clip_by_value(t, clip_value_min=-1, clip_value_max=1)
  >>> t2.numpy()
  array([[-1., -1.,  0.],
         [ 0.,  1.,  1.]], dtype=float32)

  The min and max can be the same size as `t`, or broadcastable to that size.

  >>> t = tf.constant([[-1, 0., 10.], [-1, 0, 10]])
